# Default build context ignore. Applies when no per-Dockerfile ignore
# file is present (e.g. `docker build .` or `docker build -f Dockerfile .`).
# The runtime image COPYs the Go source tree to build the binary, so
# this file is a denylist of things that must never reach the image:
# gitignored secrets, the internal vault, CI metadata, local build
# artifacts, and the other Dockerfiles used by the install-sh test
# (those have their own per-Dockerfile ignore files).
#
# The install-sh test Dockerfiles use the restrictive per-file ignores
# (Dockerfile.install-sh-cap.dockerignore, Dockerfile.install-sh-no-sha.dockerignore)
# that allow only install.sh in context.

# Source repo metadata and tooling
.git/
.github/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
.DS_Store

# Internal vault (gitignored)
DOCS/

# Secrets (gitignored)
.env
.env.*
*.token
.mcpregistry_*_token

# Local build artifacts
aguara-mcp
mcp-aguara
dist/

# Test files: not needed at runtime, reduces image size
*_test.go

# Other Dockerfiles + their per-file ignores
Dockerfile.install-sh-cap
Dockerfile.install-sh-no-sha
Dockerfile.install-sh-cap.dockerignore
Dockerfile.install-sh-no-sha.dockerignore
